<title>USA: Interstate Bakeries Corp Q4 May 31 net up.</title>
<headline>Interstate Bakeries Corp Q4 May 31 net up.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>(000'S EXCEPT PER SHARE DATA)</p>
<p>			Twelve Weeks Ended  Fifty-Two Weeks Ended</p>
<p>		     5/31/97    6/1/96	 5/31/97    6/1/96</p>
<p> Net sales	    $755,170 $ 745,720  $ 3,212,431 $2,878,180</p>
<p> Cost of products    360,370   365,639    1,566,265  1,453,191</p>
<p>Selling, delivery,</p>
<p> administrative cost 315,730   322,620    1,352,026  1,236,586</p>
<p> Other charges		 -     9,500		-	9,500</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>  amortization	  24,056    24,131	102,997    100,145</p>
<p> Operating income     55,014    23,830	191,143     78,758</p>
<p> Net income	     29,639     8,476	 97,177     24,463</p>
<p> Earnings per share     0.77	0.23	   2.55	 0.70</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	   38,274    37,650	 38,100     34,984</p>
<p>NOTE: Results for 52 weeks ended June 1, 1996, include operations of Continental Baking Co from acquisition date of July 22, 1995.</p>
<p>Year-ago Q4 and fiscal year results include after-tax charge of $5,738,000 or $0.15 a share from payment due a union-administered, multi-employer pension plan that failed.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
